{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration policy in compact specification automata. The policy gives clear priority to forward progress in clear space, uses brief directed turns for side/front obstacles, reserves backward motion only for front-obstacle recovery, and reserves full_rotate only for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path. Action states are one-shot, obstacle-triggered states never enable forward/random_walk, and uncontrollable events are total in every specification state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation in G; encode safe exploration and recovery sequencing in E",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward with occasional random_walk, while using short directed turns for obstacle recovery and a dedicated stuck->full_rotate fallback only after repeated front blockage"
  ],
